  "label": "U.S. presidents are mapped onto crackers",
  "description": "The text 'a short history of u.s. presidents' explicitly frames the visual arrangement of various crackers as a metaphor for U.S. presidents. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual material (crackers) is projected onto the textual concept (U.S. presidents), implying that the presidents are being trivialized or reduced to snack foods. The spatial arrangement of the crackers in columns further suggests a chronological or categorical progression, reinforcing the metaphorical mapping.",
